  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nFix the string representation (repr) of `T` and `S` expressions so that slice indices render as `[1:]` instead of the default Python slice repr.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\nassert repr(T['a'].b.c()) == \"T['a'].b.c()\"\nassert repr(T[1:]) == \"T[1:]\"\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Keep the public API of `glom.core` unchanged; do not rename or remove `T`, `S`, `Path`, or their existing public methods.\n- Files in scope: `glom/__init__.py`, `glom/core.py`, `glom/grouping.py`, `glom/matching.py`, `glom/mutation.py`, `glom/reduction.py`, `glom/streaming.py`, `glom/test/test_path_and_t.py`.\n\n## How success is measured\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q glom/test/test_path_and_t.py::test_path_t_roundtrip\n```",
